<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5546] Support to cancel asynchronous query job based on the asynchronous query id</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5546</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Issues&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Issues&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, Kylin has no open APIs to cancel/kill the asynchronous running query, users have to dig into the log and find out the Spark process, then to kill the process manually.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without the entrypoint to kill the running asynchronous queries, the server will lose control of resources, finally enter into a unstable state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I think it&apos;s great for Kylin to supply such an open API, to cancel/kill the asynchronous submitted queries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Proposalchanges&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposal changes&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Supply a &lt;b&gt;DELETE&lt;/b&gt; REST API &lt;tt&gt;/async_query/stop/{query_id:.+&lt;/tt&gt;}&#160;to kill the submitted asynchronous query by the&#160;&lt;tt&gt;query id&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
